1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,800
So before we even talk about this discipline don't ever be afraid to start anything.
所以，甚至在谈自律之前，永远不要害怕开始做任何事。

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:09,319
There's no reason to be afraid because nobody will ever say all the right things to the right people.
没什么好怕的，因为没人能永远对合适的人说出所有合适的话。

3
00:00:09,319 --> 00:00:14,040
Everyone has said something very embarrassing and it's better to say something than nothing at all.
每个人都说过很尴尬的话；但说点什么总比什么都不说好。

4
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:19,639
Everyone has made mistakes and that shouldn't scare you into becoming a hermit and not do anything with your life.
每个人都犯过错，这不该把你吓得变成隐士，人生什么事都不做。

5
00:00:19,639 --> 00:00:27,880
Take calculated chances meaning that with anything that you do make sure that all the upsides are better than the downsides and move on if you need to.
要审慎地冒险：无论做什么，都确保收益大于坏处，必要时就向前走。

6
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:32,400
You will know in your heart if you will regret it if you didn't take that chance on your yourself.
如果不为自己争取那个机会会后悔，你心里会知道（字幕保留重复 yourself 起句）。

7
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:40,040
Life is too short you guys there is really no reason to hold back on anything and don't ever take yourself too seriously be a bit unserious.
人生太短了，朋友们，真的没理由总缩手缩脚；也别太把自己当回事，轻松一点。

8
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:45,639
The specific person that you're so into for example is probably just afraid of coming off awkward and as nervous as you are.
比如，你特别喜欢的那个人，可能也像你一样紧张，怕自己显得尴尬。

9
00:00:45,639 --> 00:00:51,840
And so much easier set than done but just by putting yourself out there and taking the first step to do anything at all.
这说来容易做来难（字幕为 set than done），但只要你敢走出去，迈出开始做事的第一步，

10
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:56,199
You're doing way better than the other 90 of people who are just too afraid to even try.
你就已经比另外那些连尝试都不敢的人做得好多了——她说是另外的“90”。

11
00:00:56,199 --> 00:01:03,000
But guys let's face it once you start you need to have discipline and discipline is all about the habit for performing game.
但朋友们，面对现实：一旦开始，你需要自律，而自律全在于“habit for performing game”（字幕待核）。

12
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:08,240
That's really what it is discipline is what's going to carry you through even when you don't feel like it.
就是这样。即使你不想做，自律也会支撑你走下去。

13
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:15,319
You are the gamer and every time you choose discipline you win that day and day by day you build it up incrementally.
你是玩家；每次选择自律，你就赢下了那一天，一天天逐步积累。

14
00:01:15,319 --> 00:01:19,160
But you can't have it if you don't mentally and internally shift.
但如果你没有在心理和内在发生转变，你就无法拥有它。

15
00:01:19,160 --> 00:01:21,629
Sometimes you just have to stop feeling sorry for yourself.
有时，你就是得停止自怜。

16
00:01:21,639 --> 00:01:26,590
Like whatever it is that you're lacking everyone lacks something but so what.
无论你缺什么，每个人都缺点什么，那又怎样？

17
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:32,560
Stop the victim mentality and actually change in the inside so that you can move on and focus on the discipline aspect of it.
停下受害者心态，从内部真正改变，然后向前走，关注自律这一面。

18
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:39,600
So after I read these two books and they're called atomic habits and the slight edge I was totally sold on the idea of incremental progress.
所以，在读完《原子习惯》和《The Slight Edge》这两本书之后，我完全认可了渐进进步这个想法。

19
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:42,959
It's the only thing that has ever worked for me and it makes sense.
这是唯一曾对我有效的东西，而且说得通。

20
00:01:42,959 --> 00:01:47,120
Forget about all these magical quantum leaps that solve everything overnight.
别去想那些能一夜之间解决一切的神奇量子跃迁。

21
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:54,160
The only overnight solution is your self assumption your self concept that's the true quantum leap.
唯一一夜奏效的东西，是你的自我假定、自我概念——那才是真正的量子跃迁。

22
00:01:54,160 --> 00:02:00,949
Everything else is just straight bs if you're waiting for motivation to get you started stop it it's too fickle.
其余都是胡扯。如果你在等动力带你开始，别等了，它太善变了。

23
00:02:00,959 --> 00:02:07,000
Motivation can be good if it's there already but it shouldn't be the entire foundation of the habits that you're creating.
动力已经在那里时，当然可以很好，但它不该成为你正在建立的习惯的全部基础。

24
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Because motivation doesn't last and it definitely won't be there for you every single day.
因为动力不会一直持续，也肯定不会每天都在。

25
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:18,360
And when it's gone you also lose all the habits that you buil on top of it so build habits based on discipline and willpower.
它一消失，你在它上面“buil”的习惯也会失去。所以，要基于自律和意志力来建立习惯。

26
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:23,240
The key distinction isn't telling yourself I'm going to exercise for 30 minutes every day because I want to be healthy.
关键区别不是对自己说：“我每天要锻炼三十分钟，因为我想健康。”

27
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:28,440
But rather it's saying I'm going to discipline myself to work out every day because that is simply who I am.
而是说：“我要约束自己每天锻炼，因为这就是我这样的人。”

28
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:34,040
And that's my purpose and because I have purpose I also have enough willpower to always be doing that.
“那是我的目标；因为有了目标，我也有足够意志力一直做下去。”

29
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:38,280
Whatever your goals are make it so that the only way you can't lose is if you don't do it.
不管目标是什么，要让它变成这样：“你唯一不会输的情况，就是你不去做”（原字幕与下文相矛盾）。

30
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:44,400
Even if it's just doing one pushup a day make your goals so achievable and so easy that there's no way you can fail.
哪怕只是一天做一个俯卧撑，也要让目标容易实现、容易到没有失败的可能。

31
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:49,720
As long as you try and you see progress some might even say well doing one pushup won't make a difference.
只要尝试，你就能看到进步。有人可能会说：“做一个俯卧撑又不会有区别。”

32
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:55,959
I mean maybe if you only do it one time but the reality is that you probably go beyond doing one push up.
我的意思是，如果只做一次也许如此，但实际上你可能会做得超过一个。

33
00:02:55,959 --> 00:02:58,639
So there's this one trick I learned from atomic habits is where.
所以，有个我从《原子习惯》学到的小窍门：

34
00:02:58,639 --> 00:03:03,280
If you just put on sneakers to go to the gym you will already have won half the battle.
只要穿上运动鞋准备去健身房，你就已经赢了一半。

35
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:05,879
That alone will make you want to be at the gym.
仅仅这件事就会让你想去健身房。

36
00:03:05,879 --> 00:03:08,840
Once you have the willpower to get down the push up stance and complete one.
一旦你有意志力俯身摆好俯卧撑姿势，做完一个，

37
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:12,639
You will often find yourself thinking well I can do another one and I can do another one.
你常会发现自己在想：“我还能再来一个，还能再来一个。”

38
00:03:12,639 --> 00:03:16,759
So you'll probably exit your target which not only will boost your confidence to do even more.
这样你可能会“exit your target”（原字幕如此），不仅让你更有信心多做一点，

39
00:03:16,759 --> 00:03:18,840
But it will also give you a sense of accomplishment.
也会让你有成就感。

40
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:25,629
If you remember anything at all just remember the one thing that I'm saying in this video you can't fail unless you don't do it.
如果要记住什么，就记住我视频里这一点：只要你去做，你就不会失败。

41
00:03:25,639 --> 00:03:32,319
There's no reason to be afraid of failure like the most successful people that we all know has failed harder than anyone.
没理由害怕失败；我们知道的最成功的那些人，失败得比谁都惨。

42
00:03:32,319 --> 00:03:36,319
And guys I'll let you in on a huge secret I'm a loser I lose a lot.
朋友们，告诉你们一个大秘密：我是个输家，我输过很多次。

43
00:03:36,319 --> 00:03:40,830
But what matters is and the only thing that matters is I win a lot more than I lose.
但重要的是，唯一重要的是，我赢的次数比输的多得多。
